{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01361",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 9.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.82,
      "end_seconds": 14.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Okay, good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.55,
      "end_seconds": 18.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "I'm here because of irregular periods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.18,
      "end_seconds": 23.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.07,
      "end_seconds": 30.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Around four weeks... no wait, it's more like about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.06,
      "end_seconds": 34.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Yes. How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.47,
      "end_seconds": 45.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.28,
      "text": "It feels mild to me. I've also had acne, since yesterday. And I've been putting on weight as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.15,
      "end_seconds": 51.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.62,
      "end_seconds": 55.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.77,
      "end_seconds": 66.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.6,
      "end_seconds": 71.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 74.04,
      "end_seconds": 79.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 50 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.22,
      "end_seconds": 84.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.93,
      "end_seconds": 100.45,
      "duration_seconds": 14.52,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. Febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day. Right, I do miss it now and then, to be fair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.82,
      "end_seconds": 104.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.72,
      "end_seconds": 110.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Yes, I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.08,
      "end_seconds": 115.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.34,
      "end_seconds": 125.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "Heart failure, for nearly five years. I've had gout for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.05,
      "end_seconds": 127.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.33,
      "end_seconds": 132.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.1,
      "end_seconds": 137.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.87,
      "end_seconds": 144.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.73,
      "end_seconds": 150.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.7,
      "end_seconds": 155.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.11,
      "end_seconds": 160.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "So, are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.71,
      "end_seconds": 163.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.21,
      "end_seconds": 166.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.86,
      "end_seconds": 171.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.91,
      "end_seconds": 179.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "And what about headaches, milky nipple discharge or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.38,
      "end_seconds": 184.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Well, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.84,
      "end_seconds": 192.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.2,
      "end_seconds": 196.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.37,
      "end_seconds": 200.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.82,
      "end_seconds": 203.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 209.0,
      "end_seconds": 215.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Blood pressure 114 over 68, respiratory rate 16, pulse 81."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.96,
      "end_seconds": 216.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.69,
      "end_seconds": 222.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.58,
      "end_seconds": 225.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.64,
      "end_seconds": 247.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Your weight is up a little, and there is acne on the jaw and some coarse hairs on the chin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.59,
      "end_seconds": 255.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.51,
      "end_seconds": 279.32,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be polycystic ovary syndrome, or it might be high prolactin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.99,
      "end_seconds": 284.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.32,
      "end_seconds": 300.5,
      "duration_seconds": 15.18,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like polycystic ovary syndrome. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had irregular periods for about two weeks, mild, and no palpitations or milky nipple discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.39,
      "end_seconds": 304.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.37,
      "end_seconds": 345.42,
      "duration_seconds": 26.05,
      "text": "What I'm giving you is metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, long term. That's for polycystic ovaries. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.13,
      "end_seconds": 348.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.25,
      "end_seconds": 356.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "I'd like you back after the results. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.01,
      "end_seconds": 361.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.35,
      "end_seconds": 364.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}